=== student sigma RE
drmTMB(bf(yt ~ x, sigma ~ 1 + (1 | g), nu ~ 1), family = student(), data = d) 
  REFUSED/ERROR: Non-Gaussian `sigma` random effects are not implemented for `student()`. ✖ Unsupported random-effect term: `(1 | g)`. ℹ This slice adds only ordinary Student-t `mu` random intercepts;   residual-scale random effects need their own likelihood and recovery tests. 

=== student nu RE
drmTMB(bf(yt ~ x, sigma ~ 1, nu ~ 1 + (1 | g)), family = student(), data = d) 
  REFUSED/ERROR: Shape random effects are not implemented. ✖ The `nu` formula contains a random-effect bar term. ℹ Keep shape formulas fixed-effect for now, such as `nu ~ x`. ℹ Student-t `nu` models tail shape; skew-normal fixed-effect `nu` models   residual slant; skew-normal and skew-t shape random effects need separate   likelihood recovery before fitting. ℹ Latent group-level skewness, such as future `skew(id) ~ x`, remains   design-only until simulations separate it from residual skewness and   heteroscedasticity. 

