  FITTED. logLik = -414.013377128  df = 5 
   beta_mu    beta_mu beta_sigma beta_sd_mu beta_sd_mu 
  0.990562   0.468754  -0.135760  -0.386599   0.178791 

=== sd(g) ~ x (row-level covariate, varies within group)
drmTMB(bf(y ~ x + (1 | g), sigma ~ 1, sd(g) ~ x), family = gaussian(), data = d) 
  REFUSED/ERROR: `sd(g)` formulas are group-level random-effect scale models. ✖ Predictor x varies within g level "1". ℹ Use predictors that are constant within g, or use `sigma ~ x` for   observation-level residual scale. 

=== sd(g) ~ w, poisson
drmTMB(bf(yp ~ x + (1 | g), sd(g) ~ w), family = poisson(), data = d) 
  REFUSED/ERROR: Random-effect scale formulae are not implemented for Poisson models. ℹ Poisson models currently have no fitted `sigma` parameter. 

=== sd(g) ~ w, nbinom2
drmTMB(bf(yc ~ x + (1 | g), sigma ~ 1, sd(g) ~ w), family = nbinom2(), data = d) 
  REFUSED/ERROR: Random-effect scale formulae are not implemented for `nbinom2()` models. ℹ Start with fixed-effect count formulas such as `bf(count ~ x, sigma ~ z)`. 

=== sd(g) ~ w with REML
drmTMB(bf(y ~ x + (1 | g), sigma ~ 1, sd(g) ~ w), family = gaussian(), data = d, REML = TRUE) 
  REFUSED/ERROR: `REML` is not implemented with direct ordinary random-effect scale formulae yet. ℹ Use a phylogenetic direct-SD scale (`sd_phylo(...) ~ ...`), ordinary location   random effects, or set `REML = FALSE`. 

